@page "/"

<PageTitle>BlazorIslands QuickStart</PageTitle>

<h1>BlazorIslands QuickStart</h1>

<p>Three ways to use JavaScript in Blazor. Each works with static SSR, enhanced navigation, streaming and every interactive render mode, under a strict Content-Security-Policy.</p>

<ul>
    <li><a href="js-component">JS component</a>: a Razor component with a JavaScript half (<code>@@inherits JSComponent</code> + <code>.razor.js</code>).</li>
    <li><a href="island">Preact island</a>: a UI rendered by JavaScript, no build step.</li>
    <li><a href="page-script">Page script</a>: page JavaScript that runs like on a full page load.</li>
</ul>

<p>Open the browser console and run <code>BlazorIslands.print()</code> to see every island on the page.</p>
